  {"comment": "Page 7 of the painter's manual, the filters. At 1280 by 1024 and an interface scale of 1, the size page 1 is shot at. The dockers are parked and two are placed, so the canvas and the filter windows are clear. A small picture is painted with the brush, Filter, Browse Filters... is opened by its row, Box blur's window is opened, moved and cancelled, then opened again, attached and applied, and the attached row is picked, switched off and pressed twice. The filter windows are embedded windows an injected click does not reach, so their own steps drive them. The last steps press the Layers docker's delete button with the filter picked. The shots are the pictures on manual/07-filters.md, and the dumps are where the page read every name it gives."},
